    (noble ships it commented). NOTE: this is the **systemd** user.conf, not
    a limits.d file.
  - `/etc/sysctl.conf` lost `fs.file-max=5000000000` + `vm.swappiness=25`.
  - `/etc/security/limits.conf` lost 4× `nofile 10000000` lines (`*`+`andrei`,
    soft+hard) — **recoverable from the etc tarball** (an earlier "unrecoverable"
    note was wrong). `/etc/security/limits.d/` was empty on jammy.
  - `/etc/ssh/sshd_config` verified IDENTICAL to backup (earlier "missing"
    alarm was /tmp cleanup between extracts).
- llama serve restarted post-upgrade with `-c 76800 --spec-draft-n-max 3
  --chat-template-kwargs {"reasoning_effort":"high"}` (PID 14788 at the time;
  it serves OpenCode — never pkill mid-session). Canonical flag set is
  Andrei's call (old: `-c 81920 --spec-draft-n-max 2`).
- Ollama disabled (service), binary + 17G models still on disk.

### Ghostty 1.3.1 (source-built, 2026-11-15)
- 1.0.1 (jammy GTK 4.6.9 build) segfaults on noble's GTK runtime 4.14.2 →
  1.3.1 built from source; 1.4 needs GTK 4.18 (absent on noble).
- Build: Zig 0.15.2, `zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast -fno-sys=gtk4-layer-shell`.
  **Gotcha:** system integrations toggle via `-fsys=<name>` / `-fno-sys=<name>`
  (`zig build -h`), NOT `-D<name>`. zig-out gives `lib/` + `bin/`; no sudo
  needed (layer-shell built from source). Tree+log: `~/work/ghostty-131/`.
- Install: `~/.local/bin/ghostty` wrapper → `ghostty.real`;
  `~/.local/lib/ghostty/libgtk4-layer-shell.so` (+ retired `noegl.{c,so}`).
  **RUNPATH gotcha:** binary RUNPATH is the CWD-relative zig build cache →
  the wrapper's `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` is mandatory.
- **noegl shim RETIRED:** on noble GTK 4.14.2 the EGL path gives OpenGL 4.6
  (jammy's 4.6.9 EGL gave only 3.2 — that's why the shim existed).
- `~/.dotfiles/script/install-ghostty.sh` is the generic installer; do NOT run
  it on this box (would clobber the wrapper scheme; its `install_gl_shim`
  doesn't exist). Full history: `~/work/ai-tools/notes/ghostty-ubuntu2204-nvidia.md`.

## Tooling gotchas (this box)
- `sudo printf ... >> /etc/file` fails (Permission denied): the `>>` is
  performed by the USER's shell, not by sudo. Use `printf ... | sudo tee -a
  /etc/file` instead (hit live 2026-11-15, Phase 4 of the noble upgrade).
- zsh shell wrapper mangles `[[ ]]` in one-liners → write multi-line scripts
  (see AGENTS.md)
- `swapon --show=NAME,USED` unsupported — use bare `swapon --show`
- `... | head` masks the real exit code — capture to a file, check rc
- `dmesg` denied as non-root (Operation not permitted)
- After any large *scripted* apt transaction, check the `Commandline:` line in
  `/var/log/apt/history.log` — quoting bugs make excludes/flags silently no-op
  (happened with `APT::Get::Exclude`, 2026-11-14)
- pgrep/pkill self-match: bracket trick `powerline[-]daemon` in manual commands
